    "abstract": "National identification is a process through which citizens create a mental contact with the national identity they belong to. It is one of the important tasks of modern nations and states to enhance this cohesion and centripetal force. Mass media is the main channel and carrier of national identification in this process. Inaugurated in May 1936,Shanghai Sketch was one of the most important publications in the comic circle at that time. With the ever increasing national crisis,it voluntarily transferred the raising of people’s national awareness to its focus of national salvation through arts. With figuratively artistic language and expressions,it took the concepts of people and nation as narration themes,whose propagation enabled readers to develop identification with their nation and state. These efforts greatly mobilized public opinions for the following full-scale Anti-Japanese War.",
